  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for `NRS_484B_227_1_o2` (7 witnesses), using 4 of the 6 runs. I wasted one run: I ran the gate a second time before making any edit.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o2.lean`):\n- **Class:** the vehicle aggregate, `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies a highway h that has a median or divider lying on it, and the subject is not occupying an intersection on that same highway.\n- **Obligation:** h is picked out again by those same three conditions, as the record requires. For every median or divider on it, the subject's footprint must not overlap it unless the divider has the opening attribute (an opening or crossover).\n- I added no readings of my own to the rule.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_227_1_o2.lean`) are the six planned scenes plus one extra, `branch_3`:\n- The third run returned `VACUOUS`. Repeating the intersection exception in the obligation never changed a result while each scene had only one highway.\n- In `branch_3` the subject straddles two divided highways and is in an intersection that lies on only one of them. The exception lifts the duty on that highway, and the duty on the other is kept and met. This keeps the record's full re-selection of h and gives those leaves something to test.\n- Where a body straddles two regions, I listed occupancy explicitly in each scene instead of deriving it from the vehicle's position.\n\nAt one point I tried a `grep` over Core. It was blocked because only the gate command may run here, so I read the Core files with the Read tool instead.\n\nThe full log and choices are in `results/full221-1116-1018/iter-002/code/NRS_484B_227_1_o2/task_result.md`.",
